Full Vulkan matches the first three CPU token IDs. It then diverges.
The mean eight-token decode time is 1.599761 seconds on CPU and
0.316712 seconds on Vulkan. Vulkan is 5.05 times faster for this run,
but exact eight-token output parity is not achieved.

Disabling fused Gated DeltaNet in the llama.cpp context did not change
the Vulkan token sequence. The two unfused runs measured 0.353756 and
0.350348 seconds.

Partial Vulkan offload also diverged after the first three token IDs.
With 20 layers offloaded, decode took 0.820513 seconds. One offloaded
layer took 1.881422 seconds, which was slower than CPU.
